sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: swamp/workflows/workflow-operation-task-vm-upcloud-image-build.yaml, docs/reference/compute-drivers.md#build-the-upcloud-template and #sweep-upcloud, docs/cli/tasks/vm-image-build.mmd (the Incus build that this one follows), docs/cli/README.md design rules R2-R4.
  %% Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06): the UpCloud template is built with the same Ansible phases as the Incus task image and as Nodes; no orbit-agent in the build or in the template. Nick decided this; the points below that the decision leaves open are marked in the same way.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 4 (no Gateway reads or progress writes from steps), 15 (no `admit` step), 3 (no in-run leftover sweep: the host sweep owns it), 1 and 19 (`delete-builder`, `delete-smoke` fold into the cleanup; one host key pair serves both servers), 9 (one listing after the build feeds the end check and the cleanup), 18 (cleanup and prune as one forEach), 22 (curl on 209, guest work as Ansible and `@swamp/ssh exec` argv).
  %% Kept: JSON answers of UpCloud need TypeScript, so `Read the template` and `Plan the cleanup` stay. TypeScript shapes request bodies and reads answers; it makes no request.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · UpCloud template build for a recipe
  %% kind: task_vm.upcloud_image_build
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane UC icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  %% lane G icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>serve on Node 209
  participant UC as UpCloud API<br/>HTTPS from 209
  participant G as Build servers<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Admit attempt 9<br/>UpCloud · task #5182
  %%> Started by:
  %%> - `php artisan task-vms:build-upcloud-image`, `task-vms:build-recipe --retry` or `--rebuild`, or `RefreshUpCloudTaskVmBaseImage` when no verified template matches the deployed recipe
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - UpCloud is configured and no other UpCloud build runs; the ledger records attempt 9 before any remote work
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Gateway generates one ed25519 host key pair for the build servers and keeps it encrypted on the attempt
  %%> - at the run start it copies the UpCloud token and the private host key into the vault (R3), and refuses with `task_vm.image_build_superseded` when the recipe changed
  %%> - the intent holds the recipe document, identity, stamp, public host key, 209's SSH identity, the Pi pin and where the Pi build lives, the Vite+ lock, and the templates pinned by live VMs
  %%> - no agent pin, no agent envelope and no phase unit: the guest runs no agent command
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>task-vm-upcloud-image-build
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - `operation_id`, `node_id`, `kind`, the full public `intent`, and vault key names only: `task-vm-upcloud-token`, `task-vm-image-bootstrap-9`
  %%> Runs as:
  %%> - every step on 209 (`labels: {role: swamp}`), not on the Gateway Node's worker (R4)
  SW->>UC: Launch the builder<br/>POST /server
  %%> How:
  %%> - child `task-vm-upcloud-image-server`: one inline `curl` on 209 reads the plans, TypeScript shapes the body, one `curl` posts it; the token and the private host key reach curl through `--variable`, never argv
  %%> - stock UpCloud Ubuntu 26.04 template, builder user-data with the admitted host key and the `orbit` account at UID and GID 1000, label `orbit-task-image=<stamp>`
  %%> - the create answer holds the UUID and the public IPv4 address
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the server UUID, its storage and its address
  SW->>G: Run the task image phases<br/>Ansible · same as Nodes
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - child `task-vm-upcloud-image-ansible`: Swamp on 209 runs `ansible-playbook` straight to the public address of the server with the admitted host key pinned in a known-hosts file; there is no jump host
  %%> - it starts with the wait for the new server: Ansible's `wait_for_connection` until SSH answers, then `cloud-init status --wait --long` under a literal timeout
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - exit 2 of `cloud-init status` (done with recoverable errors) passes, and the check phase is the check of the server; the wait moved here from the launch because OpenSSH retries only a failed connect, and a banner exchange that fails with "No route to host" ended the third build
  %%> - the phases of the task VM role, in order: software (apt sources and packages, JavaScript, Rust, Pi), tools (the shape-gate linters), check
  %%> - versions come from the recipe document in the intent; the same playbook builds the Incus image and converges a running task VM
  %%> - the check phase also asserts that `orbit` has UID and GID 1000
  %%> - the pinned Pi build comes first: `@swamp/ssh copy` takes it from the Gateway Node to 209, `sha256sum -c` checks its pin, and the software phase copies it to the server
  %%> Replaces:
  %%> - the chunked `pi.receive-artifact` and `pi.install-artifact` of the agent
  SW->>G: Prepare and clean<br/>Ansible · clean phase
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - the same child with the tag `clean`: mask `systemd-firstboot.service`, `apt-daily.timer`, `apt-daily-upgrade.timer`, `motd-news.timer` and `unattended-upgrades.service`
  %%> - ufw on, default deny incoming, only `orbit:public-ssh-recovery` (22/tcp) open
  %%> - refuses a server that was enrolled (`/etc/orbit/agent/secret` or `/etc/wireguard/orbit.conf`), removes the build records and shell histories, and empties `/tmp` and `/var/tmp` except `systemd-private-*` and the temp directory of the running Ansible module (`ansible_*`), rotates and trims the journal and the logs
  %%> - last: the SSH host keys and the keys of `authorized_keys`, then `cloud-init clean --logs --seed --machine-id --configs all`; the Ansible session stays open through them
  %%> Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review:
  %%> - the clean list lives in the role as the `clean` phase and runs on UpCloud only; the Incus clean child keeps its own argv list. One list for both is a later step
  %%> - no recipe marker and no `image.verify`: the check phase is the one check of the role, and nothing reads the marker
  SW->>UC: Make the template<br/>stop · templatize
  %%> How:
  %%> - one soft stop with UpCloud's own 150-second hard-stop fallback, then the templatize request as `orbit-task-base-<stamp>-unverified`
  %%> - UpCloud refuses templatize until the server has stopped and changes nothing; curl's own bounded retry under one literal `timeout` is the wait (Q-WAIT), no script polls
  Note over SW: Read the template<br/>template_uuid
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - TypeScript on 209 reads the template UUID and title from the templatize answer
  %%> Returns:
  %%> - the template UUID, which the Gateway reads from this step's output (rule 4)
  SW->>UC: Smoke the template<br/>launch from template · checks
  %%> How:
  %%> - child `task-vm-upcloud-image-smoke`: the same server child with the task VM user-data and the same host key; the create waits with curl's bounded retry while UpCloud still prepares the template
  %%> - boots as in step 3, then the child `task-vm-upcloud-image-ansible` runs the `check` phase and the `template` phase against it; the `template` phase asserts that ufw is on, denies incoming connections by default and has the recovery rule
  %%> - the builder stays until the cleanup removes it
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a failed smoke check stops the build before promotion
  SW->>UC: Promote the template<br/>PUT title, labels
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - sets the `orbit.recipe` and `orbit-task-image` labels and renames the template to `orbit-task-base-<stamp>`; a PUT is safe to repeat, so curl retries while the smoke clone still holds the template
  SW->>UC: List servers, templates<br/>settle · always
  %%> When:
  %%> - after the build job, whatever its outcome, with the condition `always` (rule 19)
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one listing of the servers labelled `orbit-task-image` and of the account's templates
  %%> Why:
  %%> - it finds this attempt's servers also when a create answer or a child's output was lost
  Note over SW: Plan the cleanup<br/>promoted · deletes
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - TypeScript on 209 confirms the promoted title and labels, and picks what goes: this attempt's two servers; after promotion, verified templates beyond the two newest that no live VM pins; otherwise this attempt's unverified template
  Note over SW: Check the template<br/>assert
  %%> End check:
  %%> - after a successful build, the native `assert` checks that the listed promoted template is the one templatize made; this is the one end check (rule 9)
  SW->>UC: Delete servers, templates<br/>cleanup · forEach
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - one `forEach` over the plan; each started server gets a hard stop, then one `DELETE` with its storage, which curl retries while UpCloud still stops it (Q-WAIT)
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - best effort with `allowFailure` (rule 10): the run's outcome stays, and the next host sweep removes what stays
  alt template promoted
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>template_uuid
    Note over GW: Record attempt 9<br/>succeeded · template verified
    %%> Result:
    %%> - new UpCloud claims for this recipe use the template
  else a step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    Note over GW: Mark attempt 9 failed<br/>previous template stays
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the failed step names its own code; reconcile alerts for the identity; `task-vms:build-recipe --retry` records a new attempt
  end
